00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.681
understand how all my different
market segments were doing,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.180
how my advertisements
are performing

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.861
across all the different
channels I was spending money

00:00:52.861 --> 00:00:53.360
across?

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.530
Hello.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.660
Invest in the most
promising opportunities.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.640
If you're in the
advertising space,

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.520
there's been an old joke.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.830
I know 50% of my
ad spend is wasted.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.900
I just don't know which 50%.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.210
So how do you identify
which 50% is doing well,

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.539
which one's not doing well?

00:01:20.539 --> 00:01:22.580
And finally, how do you
understand your customer?

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:26.030
How do you understand and
profile your ideal customer?

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.890
How do you improve the
targeting for that.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.270
And so you want to find--

00:01:32.714 --> 00:01:33.214
sorry.

00:01:33.214 --> 00:01:36.176
I'm just going to skip this.

00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:37.800
So these are the
things you want to do,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.890
but these are the
challenges I face.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.920
So data lives in silos.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.440
If you're advertising
with us on Google,

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.680
you already know that, say,
on AdWords or DoubleClick, DFP

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.630
or YouTube, these are
all individual silos

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.940
you need to connect to
and pull into one place

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.290
to get visibility
into your customer.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.540
Now that's just for marketing.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.680
What about your own
first party data?

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.280
What about your customers,
your CRM data, purchasing,

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.150
invoicing?

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.840
How do you get that
all into one place?

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.840
It's really hard to get
insight in your customer

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.923
if you can't even get
everything in a single place

00:02:07.923 --> 00:02:10.180
to look at it.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.910
And earlier I
said, well you have

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:13.470
to make a decision
on identifying

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.900
which 50% is performing poorly
or which one is doing well.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.890
Well in the marketing space,
there's 3,000 tools for you

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:20.670
to choose from.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:24.000
So even before you decide
which 50% is good or bad,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.700
you need to make a decision as
to which tools you want to use

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.470
to help solve that problem.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.330
In terms of understanding
your customer,

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:36.600
we spoke with a large bank,
asked them this question.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.640
That was their answer.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.770
How much data, how
much customer data

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.150
do I use in my
advertising tools?

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.416
None, I can't link
the data sets.

00:02:45.416 --> 00:02:47.942
So, what do you want
to spend your time on?

00:02:47.942 --> 00:02:50.150
Do you want to be a business
owner or a data plumber?

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.440
Do you want to spend your
time running your business

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.440
or moving all the
data into one place?

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.620
Really, it shouldn't
be this hard.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.328
And this is how Cloud
would like to help.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:06.620
Earlier today we announced the
BigQuery Data Transfer Service.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.840
What it is is a data
movement service

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.030
from our largest
advertising platforms

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:14.039
into BigQuery on a
scheduled managed basis.

00:03:14.039 --> 00:03:16.580
If you're a customer of AdWords,
DoubleClick, Bid or Campaign

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.520
Manager, DoubleClick for
Publishers or YouTube,

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.860
today you can have your
analysts move data into BigQuery

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.820
without having any
development effort required.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:32.030
Now BigQuery is just where
you load all your data.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.590
That's great in
isolation, but hey,

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.881
what if you want to get your
web traffic data in there?

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:38.280
What if you want to get your
mobile traffic in there?

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.830
Well Google Analytics
360 customers

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.230
also have direct
connectivity to BigQuery.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:46.560
And they will export their data
to BigQuery for you as well.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.560
And finally, if you're
a CMO or a marketer,

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.920
you need to do more than
just Google properties.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.000
So how do you get data from
Salesforce, Facebook, Twitter,

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.654
Marketo, MailChimp, or
Eloqua into BigQuery?

00:04:01.654 --> 00:04:03.320
We have an ecosystem
of partners for you

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.512
to work with to set
up that automated data

00:04:05.512 --> 00:04:06.470
movement into BigQuery.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.580
So we've identified
three steps to insight.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.774
The first step is collecting
all the data in one place.

00:04:15.774 --> 00:04:17.440
With the BigQuery
Data Transfer Service,

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.978
you can get AdWords,
DoubleClick for Publishers,

00:04:19.978 --> 00:04:21.519
DoubleClick Bid and
Campaign Manager,

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:23.800
and YouTube into BigQuery.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.260
With Google Analytics, they
have direct connectivity

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.712
into BigQuery as well.

00:04:27.712 --> 00:04:29.170
And for the non-Google
data sources

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:30.628
that aren't mentioned
here, you can

00:04:30.628 --> 00:04:33.190
work with our partners such
as Informatica, Segment,

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:37.980
and Funnel to get your
Salesforce data, Facebook,

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:41.341
Marketo into BigQuery as well.

00:04:41.341 --> 00:04:42.840
The second step is
then figuring out

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.360
how to make sense of it all.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.480
So once you get the data into
BigQuery, it's pretty raw.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.910
For those of you who are
advertising professionals,

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.743
you know that you have
to inject your custom

00:04:52.743 --> 00:04:55.260
IDs into, say, DoubleClick,
shows up as other data.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.390
How do you extract
that from those strings

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.880
and make use of it?

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.310
Also earlier today we
announced a product

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.202
called Cloud Dataprep, which
is a visual ETL tool that

00:05:05.202 --> 00:05:06.660
lets you clean up
that data, again,

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.880
without having to
do any programming.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.120
So your analyst can
then use Cloud Dataprep

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.740
to clean up that data,
extract those custom user IDs,

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.481
and dump that into BigQuery.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.980
If you have a data
engineering team,

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.422
we have Apache Beam
via Cloud Dataflow.

00:05:20.422 --> 00:05:22.755
If you want to do something
more sophisticated than just

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.540
a simple extraction,
you can use Dataflow

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.820
to pull the raw
data from BigQuery

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:31.860
and then dump it back in there,
cleansed and ready to go.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:34.220
And the third piece is the
analysis and visualization

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:34.850
piece.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.975
So what I want to show here
is that BigQuery is not

00:05:36.975 --> 00:05:37.940
its own island.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.570
You can of course use SQL to
analyze the data in place.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:44.990
But we also support
exports to Excel.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.020
You can also pull data
from Google Sheets.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:48.936
And for the technical
numbers of the audience,

00:05:48.936 --> 00:05:52.590
we do have JDBC and ODBC
connectivity as well.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.770
On top of that,
Dataprep does work

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:57.170
with a lot of existing
visualization partners listed

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:58.430
here.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:02.000
Tableau, Looker, Google Data
Studio, among many others,

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.052
work with BigQuery
out of the box.

00:06:06.052 --> 00:06:08.010
We're doing all of this
to accelerate your time

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.530
to insight.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:13.950
So next I'd like to hand the
mic over to a few customers

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.110
that we've invited over.

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:17.550
And we'll have
Mercedes-Benz USA come up,

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:20.160
as well as their agency,
SapientRazorfish.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.340
Then we'll transition
over to Zenith.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:26.000
And we will have a fireside chat
after that with "The New York

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:26.750
Times" and Hearst.

