00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:03.780
So it's really cool to be here.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.220
So I'll talk about
what we're doing.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:08.820
So our data, as you can
imagine like most clients,

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.030
we're getting data from all
kinds of different places--

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.390
from our websites, from our
media, from our dealerships,

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:16.280
from after-sales.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.130
I mean, it just goes on and on.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:22.810
So like Matt was saying,
most of it is in silos.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:25.680
So we're trying to
bring all that together.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.650
So what we've noticed is a
lot of the companies that

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.780
are really doing
well are working

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:33.850
on kind of like a data
as a platform space.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:36.660
So in order to do
that, our vision is

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.730
to try to be at the
intersection of,

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:43.020
not only are we superior
technology-wise,

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.640
but we can be flexible.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.420
We can be agile.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:48.180
We can be creative.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.550
We can let the data
power the decisions

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:52.200
that need to be made
to determine what

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.134
marketing strategies
we use instead of just

00:07:54.134 --> 00:07:55.800
kind of sticking our
thumb up in the air

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:58.320
and hoping that we're
targeting the right people

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:01.680
and using the right message,
and then connecting it

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.990
from all the departments
within the M-B USA.

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:07.669
So is what we're doing
helping our vans department?

00:08:07.669 --> 00:08:09.960
Is what we're doing helping
our after-sales department,

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.410
et cetera, et cetera.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.720
And then so some growth
opportunities for us

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.840
by having this connected data--

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:23.970
I mean, it's really about being
a customer-centric company.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:27.090
Matt mentioned having a
complete view of your business.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.190
So for us it's really about
having a complete view

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.130
of your customer.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:33.150
So it's getting away
from that aggregate data

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:36.830
at the broad level,
demo level, to what

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.100
is Matthew Granish doing?

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.409
Because the way I
buy a car is probably

00:08:40.409 --> 00:08:43.679
going to be different than the
way the next guy buys a car.

00:08:43.679 --> 00:08:47.610
And so we have KPI buckets
and intuition that tells us

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:50.880
that you start here and you
do this and you end up there.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.690
But in reality, everybody
does it differently.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:58.050
So we really need
to use these things

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.520
to generate internal
efficiencies

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:03.810
so we can track all of this.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.330
And so this is just kind of
reinforcing that, putting

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.600
the customer first.

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:10.910
And so this is kind
of like the path

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.520
that you could say where
most companies are probably

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:14.630
progressing.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:19.490
So we start off with a very
simple, basic, retroactive look

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.000
at what we did.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.910
And then we're trying
to build the systems

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:24.680
through the
interconnectivity that we

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:28.370
use the cloud for to get
those real time optimizations

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:32.360
and to identify what are the
things that the people who

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:35.049
are converting doing,
and how is that

00:09:35.049 --> 00:09:36.590
different than the
people who are not

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:40.370
converting so we can target the
converters more efficiently?

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:43.940
So as we get towards
the highest bar,

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:46.460
the customer centricity,
obviously there's

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.200
a lot of data that
has to be processed,

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.350
and very quickly, to
make all that happen.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.840
So you'll hear from
our data scientists

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:57.770
on why the Google
platform works so well.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:01.010
For me, it just works really
well because it's fast.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:03.370
So we don't have a
petabyte of data yet.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:06.250
But if you saw that
example at 12:00,

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:09.740
they analyzed a petabyte of data
in two minutes or something,

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:10.894
almost three minutes.

00:10:10.894 --> 00:10:12.560
So if they can do
that in three minutes,

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.140
then ours is going to
be a walk in the park.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:17.030
So that's why I'm
really happy is

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:19.580
they're able to answer the
questions that I have very

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.530
quickly and I don't
have to wait days

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:23.330
to get the information
that I need

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:25.940
to inform marketing choices.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:29.780
So just some reasons
why GCP works--

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:33.350
it's quick, it costs
less, and there's not

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:34.690
a big implementation time.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.980
Most of our systems
are already using

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:39.320
a Google product of some
sort, so the integration

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.590
was very easy for us.

