00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:52.260
And I see them as--

00:23:52.260 --> 00:23:54.900
I distinguish Google,
in particular,

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:56.850
as a partner rather than
a software supplier.

00:23:56.850 --> 00:24:01.049
And we are heavy users of their
technology, the cloud included.

00:24:01.049 --> 00:24:03.090
And there's probably many
people in this audience

00:24:03.090 --> 00:24:06.690
that would have
traditionally been AWS users.

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:08.857
And we are no different.

00:24:08.857 --> 00:24:10.440
But we didn't really
have any interest

00:24:10.440 --> 00:24:12.930
in just switching cloud
platforms if there

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:15.570
wasn't a long term benefit.

00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:18.090
And I certainly see Google
as the long term partner,

00:24:18.090 --> 00:24:19.590
particular in the
use case I'm going

00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:22.440
to talk to you about today.

00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:25.590
Particularly as a
media agency, we

00:24:25.590 --> 00:24:29.460
are heavy users of the
DoubleClick platform,

00:24:29.460 --> 00:24:32.430
and have spent many years
encouraging many of our biggest

00:24:32.430 --> 00:24:36.850
global clients to switch to
an integrated Google ad tech

00:24:36.850 --> 00:24:39.000
stack, for a lot of reasons.

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:41.820
And it's enabled us to do
some of the things I'm going

00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:44.350
to talk about in a second.

00:24:44.350 --> 00:24:47.837
So what's our particular
use case for the cloud?

00:24:47.837 --> 00:24:49.920
Well it actually involves
artificial intelligence,

00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:53.250
which you might not expect to
see from a traditional media

00:24:53.250 --> 00:24:54.450
agency.

00:24:54.450 --> 00:24:57.750
But it's because we
started to reimagine

00:24:57.750 --> 00:25:01.630
what the digital media agency
is going to be in the future.

00:25:01.630 --> 00:25:04.590
Now what we're doing here is
taking very, very granular

00:25:04.590 --> 00:25:07.110
cookie level data
from the ad server,

00:25:07.110 --> 00:25:11.070
fusing that with first party
data from all our clients,

00:25:11.070 --> 00:25:12.780
and then applying
a set of machine

00:25:12.780 --> 00:25:15.270
learning algorithms
to all of that data

00:25:15.270 --> 00:25:18.510
to determine what is it
that's driving the conversion,

00:25:18.510 --> 00:25:22.080
or whatever the
given KPI might be.

00:25:22.080 --> 00:25:25.050
But then in a world first,
we've taken that machine

00:25:25.050 --> 00:25:28.110
learning result and we've
pushed it back to DoubleClick.

00:25:28.110 --> 00:25:30.390
Now that's never been done.

00:25:30.390 --> 00:25:33.210
Now the reason we're doing
that is not because it's clever

00:25:33.210 --> 00:25:36.825
and it's technically difficult
to achieve, which it is.

00:25:36.825 --> 00:25:39.720
It's because we really want
to think about the automated

00:25:39.720 --> 00:25:42.300
digital media agency
of the future that's

00:25:42.300 --> 00:25:44.970
closed loop and
highly automated.

00:25:44.970 --> 00:25:47.040
And that's exactly what
you're seeing here.

00:25:47.040 --> 00:25:50.820
And this process started nearly
two years ago with a Aviva

00:25:50.820 --> 00:25:53.280
as the founding client.

00:25:53.280 --> 00:25:56.430
And just to give you
an example, Aviva

00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:59.820
gave us access to
their entire CRM data.

00:25:59.820 --> 00:26:02.130
And we are only the
second organization

00:26:02.130 --> 00:26:05.910
in the world to have access to
their price elasticity data.

00:26:05.910 --> 00:26:09.690
And that means we know the
connection, the relationship

00:26:09.690 --> 00:26:12.630
between the digital
traffic for an individual,

00:26:12.630 --> 00:26:16.350
their relative price elasticity,
and anything else Aviva

00:26:16.350 --> 00:26:17.740
knows about the individual.

00:26:17.740 --> 00:26:20.010
So the application
data, for example,

00:26:20.010 --> 00:26:22.500
that when you sign on
for an insurance quote,

00:26:22.500 --> 00:26:26.570
we fuse that data
together, applied a machine

00:26:26.570 --> 00:26:28.685
learning technique, and
then pushed that result

00:26:28.685 --> 00:26:29.310
to DoubleClick.

00:26:29.310 --> 00:26:31.730
We're steadily rolling
this out for a number

00:26:31.730 --> 00:26:33.890
of our global
clients, which means

00:26:33.890 --> 00:26:38.550
we need a cloud partner that
will scale with us in this way.

00:26:38.550 --> 00:26:40.960
In this particular example,
the volumes of data

00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:42.150
aren't particularly huge.

00:26:42.150 --> 00:26:44.930
We're talking about between
50 and 100 gigabytes a day.

00:26:44.930 --> 00:26:46.520
So it's not enormous.

00:26:46.520 --> 00:26:49.460
But the point is this is
for every single client.

00:26:49.460 --> 00:26:51.590
This is not one use
case for one client.

00:26:51.590 --> 00:26:56.320
This is all our
major global clients.

00:26:56.320 --> 00:26:58.364
So as we move
forward, that score

00:26:58.364 --> 00:27:00.280
that we're generating
through machine learning

00:27:00.280 --> 00:27:03.920
is now a very rich picture of
what we know about that cookie.

00:27:03.920 --> 00:27:06.070
It's what we call a smart ID.

00:27:06.070 --> 00:27:08.320
So that means that the factors
that we're passing back

00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:10.210
to DoubleClick are
a very rich picture

00:27:10.210 --> 00:27:14.200
of what role has content,
for example, played

00:27:14.200 --> 00:27:15.020
in the conversion.

00:27:15.020 --> 00:27:16.870
What role has an
individual campaign

00:27:16.870 --> 00:27:19.390
played in its conversion?

00:27:19.390 --> 00:27:23.330
And we're starting to
unpick content, for example,

00:27:23.330 --> 00:27:28.522
so assigning numerical values
to text, video, and graphics.

00:27:28.522 --> 00:27:29.980
Because we want to
understand, what

00:27:29.980 --> 00:27:33.050
is it that's really
driven the conversion?

00:27:33.050 --> 00:27:36.400
Now I'm slightly heretical
in my organization,

00:27:36.400 --> 00:27:39.490
and I don't believe that media
always drives the conversion.

00:27:39.490 --> 00:27:40.960
It absolutely doesn't.

00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:44.160
There are many other factors
that drive a conversion.

00:27:44.160 --> 00:27:46.120
And what we're
starting to unpick here

00:27:46.120 --> 00:27:48.430
is what is the
relationship between some

00:27:48.430 --> 00:27:49.930
of those other factors.

00:27:49.930 --> 00:27:52.930
And this is the primary
use case that we've

00:27:52.930 --> 00:27:55.960
applied Google Cloud.

00:27:55.960 --> 00:27:58.270
In terms of performance,
just to give you

00:27:58.270 --> 00:28:01.070
some idea of scale in
that Aviva example,

00:28:01.070 --> 00:28:03.250
this is transformational stuff.

00:28:03.250 --> 00:28:06.760
We identified 83,000 additional
quotes in our initial exercise

00:28:06.760 --> 00:28:09.600
in the first three months.

00:28:09.600 --> 00:28:12.210
And if you were to sum
this up over the course

00:28:12.210 --> 00:28:16.170
of the relationship with Aviva
just on this single project,

00:28:16.170 --> 00:28:20.660
a 15% reduction in CPA, which
for them is very significant.

00:28:20.660 --> 00:28:23.330
And they're the first
insurance organization

00:28:23.330 --> 00:28:26.960
to even attempt this.

00:28:26.960 --> 00:28:29.720
So just in terms of
specifically wrapping up

00:28:29.720 --> 00:28:32.480
on the benefits of
GCP for us, we've

00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:36.920
seen a 30% reduction in
the client setup process--

00:28:36.920 --> 00:28:39.080
which for us is
fairly significant,

00:28:39.080 --> 00:28:41.930
because use of talent
is a challenge--

00:28:41.930 --> 00:28:44.450
a 20% reduction in hardware
resource for machine learning

00:28:44.450 --> 00:28:49.760
solutions, and a 20% reduction
in computation costs.

00:28:49.760 --> 00:28:51.680
Which for us, given
the scale of what

00:28:51.680 --> 00:28:54.080
we're trying to do
across something

00:28:54.080 --> 00:28:58.690
like 150 global clients, this
is really quite significant.

00:28:58.690 --> 00:29:01.820
But probably the important thing
is, just to close, is I say

00:29:01.820 --> 00:29:06.007
Google as the partner,
not a software supplier.

00:29:06.007 --> 00:29:08.392
