00:34:16.710 --> 00:34:17.650
We had Redshift.

00:34:17.650 --> 00:34:20.130
We have on-premise Hadoop.

00:34:20.130 --> 00:34:23.210
I know who had that idea.

00:34:23.210 --> 00:34:27.350
We wanted to collect a lot of
that, put it in one, you know,

00:34:27.350 --> 00:34:31.370
this data lake
concept, put it online,

00:34:31.370 --> 00:34:35.230
make all data join away.

00:34:35.230 --> 00:34:37.760
Where we are now,
we've killed Redshift.

00:34:37.760 --> 00:34:39.520
We've shut down Hadoop.

00:34:39.520 --> 00:34:41.687
We have a fair amount
of data in BigQuery.

00:34:41.687 --> 00:34:42.520
It's up and running.

00:34:42.520 --> 00:34:43.400
We're Dataflow.

00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:45.750
We're using Pub/Sub.

00:34:45.750 --> 00:34:49.291
And BigQuery is driving a lot
of our analysis, not all of it

00:34:49.291 --> 00:34:49.790
